asons for conversion from laparoscopic to open cholecystectomy in an urban teaching hospital</article-title><source>Am J Surg</source><year>1994</year><volume>168</volume><fpage>555</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7977995</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT20"><label>20</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lau</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Brooks</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Predictive factors for unanticipated admission after ambulatory laparoscopic cholecystectomy</article-title><source>Arch Surg</source><year>2001</year><volume>136</volume><fpage>1150</fpage><lpage>3</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11585507</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT21"><label>21</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fiorillo</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>Davidson</surname><given-names>PG</given-names></name><name><surname>Fiorillo</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>D'Anna</surname><given-names>JA</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name><name><surname>Sithian</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Silich</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>149 ambulatory laparoscopic cholecystectomy</article-title><source>Surg Endosc</source><year>1996</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>52</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8711607</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT22"><label>22</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Llorente</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Laparoscopic cholecystectomy in the ambulatory surgery setting</article-title><source>J Laparoendosc Surg</source><year>1992</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>23</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1533545</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT23"><label>23</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Deziel</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Millikan</surname><given-names>KW</given-names></name><name><surname>Economou</surname><given-names>SG</given-names></name><name><surname>Doolas</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Ko</surname><given-names>ST</given-names></name><name><surname>Airan</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Complications of laparoscopic Cholecystectomy: A national survey of 4292 hospitals and an analysis of 77604 cases</article-title><source>Am J Surg</source><year>1993</year><volume>165</volume><fpage>9</fpage><lpage>14</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8418705</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="CIT24"><label>24</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Richardson</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Bell</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Fullarton</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>West of Scotland Laparoscopic Cholecystectomy Audit Group. Incidence and nature of bile duct injuries following laparoscopic Cholecystectomy: An audit of 5913 cases</article-title><source>Br J Surg</source><year>1996</year><volume>83</volume><fpage>1356</fpage><lpage>60</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8944450</pub-id></element-citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>